# Auth and Authorization

- Keep authentication and CSRF/origin enforcement in the auth middleware stack. Do not add ad hoc login gates inside unrelated blueprints when middleware already owns the request boundary.
- Preserve public-path and OPTIONS/static skip behavior explicitly. New unauthenticated routes must be intentional public exceptions, not accidental omissions.
- Authorize through the central dispatcher. No providers, or no applicable provider, means deny. Opt into `public=True` only for deliberately open capabilities.
- Compatibility providers that do not govern a capability must raise `AuthorizationNotApplicable`. Never treat abstention as success.
- Register CRUD policy through the auth provider. Generated CRUD without a governing provider stays fail-closed; do not bypass with local allowlists.
- Use `BaseSecurityCapability` / capability grants for non-CRUD route and nav permissions (`resource` + exact `action`). Keep `BaseSecurityModelRight` for generated CRUD operations. Do not map `manage`/`operate` onto model-right `write` when an exact capability definition exists.
- For sensitive-row record rules: put restrictive domain filters (for example `sensitive=False`) only on the standard users group; give elevated/Policy groups the same model rights without those hide rules. Do not dual-assign users to both groups — `apply_record_rules` ANDs all matching group rules, so dual membership still hides rows. Gate create of sensitive values via model `_crud_validate` (create ignores record-rule domains).
- Treat `managed_by` policy rows as component-owned. Mutating them through ordinary CRUD must conflict; change ownership only through security reconciliation.
- Security reconciliation claims matching rows under the advisory lock, never overwrites a different owner, and must not leave legacy NULL `managed_by` seed rows that abort addon registration.
- Keep OAuth and session secrets in approved secret settings or deployment secrets. Never log tokens, codes, cookies, or raw provider responses.
- Prefer existing session and OAuth blueprints/utils under `framework/addons/auth` over parallel auth stacks in product addons.
- When API is up but routes 404 after auth/policy changes, inspect reconciliation and migration state before networking; a reconcile `RuntimeError` aborts later blueprint registration.
